# The Xcode loop
This machine builds for every Crew at once, so every xcodebuild you skip is minutes given back to all of them.
- Build once per edit with `build-for-testing`, then run the one test you need with `test-without-building -xctestrun <file> -only-testing:<Target/Class/method>`; a full `xcodebuild test` is for the gate.
- Pass `-collect-test-diagnostics never` (two tokens) on every test run: otherwise a failed test collects a sysdiagnose for up to 600 seconds.
- One simulator for this worktree, booted once and kept warm.
- A probe test prints every value you want in one run. Kill xcodebuild as soon as its log shows `error:`.
- Never run two xcodebuilds at once.
{{- end}}
